  <title xml:lang="EN">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">RMGP: EUAA Migration Governance Programme</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="2" xml:lang="EN">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">The project&#x2019;s objective contributes to the overall development objective (i.e. Impact) of the RMGP - &#x201c;Migration management is enhanced, safe, orderly and rights-based in focus countries across the MENA region&#x201d;- and to the Specific Objective (i.e. Outcome 2): 
&#x201c;Enhanced asylum systems and processing (including documentation, registration, reception etc.)&#x201d;. 

The Agency will focus on enhancing institutional development on asylum in priority TCs through regional and national capacity building activities through a multifaceted approach aimed at strengthening legal frameworks, improving administrative processes, and building the capacities of institutions and personnel involved in asylum and reception procedures.

Overall, the EUAA intervention will be designed and implemented by considering &#x2013; as a crosscutting focus across the Outputs - the specific situation of asylum seekers which belong to vulnerable groups and particularly vulnerable sub-groups such as children on the move, including unaccompanied children, pregnant women, victims of gender-based and sexual violence, survivors of trafficking in human beings (THB).</narrative>
  </description>
